"""DYNAMIX_REPORT.html from saved artifacts (all interpretive sentences derived from numbers)."""
import json, glob, base64, pandas as pd, numpy as np, os
OUT = 'outputs'; FIG = f'{OUT}/figures_dynamix'; D = f'{FIG}/plotted_data'
cap = {**json.load(open(f'{FIG}/captions_diag.json')), **json.load(open(f'{FIG}/captions_dm.json'))}
cap.update({'figD1_conditional_sensitivity': cap.get('figD1_conditional_sensitivity')})
img = lambda n, c=None: f'<figure><img src="data:image/png;base64,{base64.b64encode(open(f"{FIG}/{n}.png","rb").read()).decode()}" style="max-width:100%"><figcaption>{c or cap[n]}</figcaption></figure>'
av = json.load(open(f'{OUT}/v2/availability_summary.json')); ce = json.load(open(f'{OUT}/v2/component_evidence_summary.json')); sb = json.load(open(f'{OUT}/dynamix/seed_budget.json')); em = json.load(open(f'{OUT}/dynamix/embed_runtime.json')); rm = json.load(open(f'{OUT}/pool/reference_mapping_summary.json'))
perm = json.load(open(f'{OUT}/dynamix/permutation_pretrained_remitter.json')); SCR = pd.read_csv(f'{D}/summary_and_intervals.csv'); PAIR = pd.read_csv(f'{D}/paired_differences.csv'); ALL = pd.read_csv(f'{D}/all_metrics.csv'); REP = pd.read_csv(f'{D}/representation_stability.csv'); SENS = pd.read_csv(f'{D}/conditional_sensitivity_E01_vs_E01c.csv'); RMF = pd.read_csv(f'{D}/reference_mapping_per_feature.csv')
CE = pd.read_csv(f'{D}/component_evidence_qc_sample.csv')
drift = CE.low_freq_fraction >= 0.95; blink = (CE.n_blinks >= 5) & (CE.blink_locked_peak_to_baseline_SD >= 3); heog = (CE.abs_r_HEOG >= 0.3)
CAT = dict(eye_locked=int((blink & ~drift).sum()), heog_only=int((~blink & heog & ~drift).sum()), drift_like=int(drift.sum()), unresolved=int((~blink & ~heog & ~drift).sum()), few_blinks_lt5=int((CE.n_blinks < 5).sum()), total=len(CE))
cap['figD2_component_evidence_example1'] = cap['figD2_component_evidence_example2'] = cap['figD2_component_evidence_example3'] = 'Documentation of components removed by v2 in the fixed-rule QC examples (IDs not shown): time course with VEOG/HEOG (bipolar), source spectrum, blink-locked average. NOTE the blink-locked averages often rest on very few detected blinks (n is printed on each panel; several have n=1), so they are weak evidence; slow-drift components (low-frequency fraction near 1.0) can correlate with EOG without being eye activity. Cleaning was not changed.'
cfgR = json.load(open(sorted(glob.glob('runs/DM_Remitter_*'))[-1] + '/config.json')); cfgP = json.load(open(sorted(glob.glob('runs/DM_Responder_*'))[-1] + '/config.json'))
fmt = lambda df: df.round(3).to_html(index=False, na_rep='undefined')
sR = SCR[SCR.endpoint == 'Remitter'].set_index('model'); pre = sR.loc['pretrained']; ra, rb, rc = (sR.loc[m] for m in ('random_a', 'random_b', 'random_c')); rnd_mean = [sR.loc[m].mean_auc for m in ('random_a', 'random_b', 'random_c')]
pr = PAIR[(PAIR.endpoint == 'Remitter')].set_index('comparison'); vs_e = pr.loc['pretrained - E01c']; sensU = SENS[(SENS.endpoint == 'Remitter') & (SENS.group == 'availability unchanged')].iloc[0]
rep = REP.groupby('model')[['split_half_SB_median', 'icc_windows_median', 'replicate_halves_r_median']].median().round(3)
bottom = (f'Pretrained DynaMix, Remitter: mean AUC {pre.mean_auc:.3f} (95% bootstrap [{pre.mean_auc_lo:.3f}, {pre.mean_auc_hi:.3f}]); repeats {pre.auc_s42:.3f}/{pre.auc_s43:.3f}/{pre.auc_s44:.3f}. Saved E01c: {sR.loc["E01c"].mean_auc:.3f}. Random-weight models: {rnd_mean[0]:.3f}, {rnd_mean[1]:.3f}, {rnd_mean[2]:.3f}. '
          f'Triage rule (mean AUC &ge; 0.60, gain &ge; 0.05 over E01c, positive in every repeat): <b>{"met" if bool(pre.triage_pass) else "not met"}</b>. Permutation test (999 permutations, plus-one p): p = {perm["p_value_plus_one"]:.3f}; null 95th percentile {perm["null_q95"]:.3f}.')
claims = f'''<table><tr><th>Question</th><th>Evidence in this stage</th><th>Reading</th></tr>
<tr><td>1. Is DynaMix a stable/useful EEG <i>representation</i>? (label-free)</td><td>Median split-half reliability {rep.loc["pretrained","split_half_SB_median"]:.2f} (pretrained) vs {rep.loc[["random_a","random_b","random_c"],"split_half_SB_median"].min():.2f}&ndash;{rep.loc[["random_a","random_b","random_c"],"split_half_SB_median"].max():.2f} (random); ICC across windows {rep.loc["pretrained","icc_windows_median"]:.2f} vs {rep.loc[["random_a","random_b","random_c"],"icc_windows_median"].min():.2f}&ndash;{rep.loc[["random_a","random_b","random_c"],"icc_windows_median"].max():.2f}</td><td>Numerically stable to gating noise (replicate r &ge; {REP.replicate_halves_r_median[REP.model=="pretrained"].min():.2f}) but NOT patient-stable across windows: median split-half reliability of the 10 latent means is at most {REP[(REP.model=="pretrained")&REP.feature.str.startswith("z")].split_half_SB_median.max():.2f}; the best feature is pretrained gate entropy ({REP[(REP.model=="pretrained")&(REP.feature=="gate_entropy")].split_half_SB_median.iloc[0]:.2f}). The summaries mostly describe the window, not a stable person trait. Says nothing about outcome.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Does it <i>predict treatment</i>?</td><td>{bottom}</td><td>Patient-level out-of-fold; exploratory; cohort previously used; session-1 timing assumed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Is there evidence that <i>pretraining helps</i>?</td><td>Pretrained minus random A/B/C mean AUC: {pr.loc["pretrained - random_a"].mean_auc_diff:+.3f} [{pr.loc["pretrained - random_a"].auc_lo:+.3f}, {pr.loc["pretrained - random_a"].auc_hi:+.3f}], {pr.loc["pretrained - random_b"].mean_auc_diff:+.3f} [{pr.loc["pretrained - random_b"].auc_lo:+.3f}, {pr.loc["pretrained - random_b"].auc_hi:+.3f}], {pr.loc["pretrained - random_c"].mean_auc_diff:+.3f} [{pr.loc["pretrained - random_c"].auc_lo:+.3f}, {pr.loc["pretrained - random_c"].auc_hi:+.3f}]</td><td>Three separate random fits shown; no averaging/selection. Pretraining was on simulated dynamical systems, not EEG.</td></tr></table>'''
tabs = ''.join(f'<h3>{e}: all repeats</h3>' + fmt(ALL[ALL.endpoint == e][['model', 'seed', 'N', 'prevalence', 'AUC', 'AP', 'nPPV', 'sensitivity', 'PPV', 'balanced_accuracy', 'Brier', 'n_pos_calls', 'TP', 'FP', 'TN', 'FN']]) for e in ('Remitter', 'Responder'))
html = f'''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>DynaMix evaluation and reference mapping</title><style>body{{font:15px/1.5 system-ui;max-width:1080px;margin:2em auto;padding:0 1em}}figcaption{{font-size:13px;color:#333}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px}}td,th{{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:2px 5px;vertical-align:top}}.box{{background:#fff4e5;border-left:4px solid #D55E00;padding:.5em 1em}}code{{font-size:12px}}</style>
<h1>DynaMix frozen evaluation and outcome-blind reference-pool mapping</h1>
<div class="box"><b>Exploratory.</b> Same 164 patients as earlier stages (not untouched); session 1 = pretreatment assumed; not a replication of Tolley et al.; not a test of superiority over E01c. {bottom}</div>
<h2>Three questions, kept separate</h2>{claims}
<h2>Decision for this stage</h2><p>The frozen DynaMix extraction does not meet the pre-set triage rule and its permutation test is non-significant; its summaries are not patient-stable across windows, which is a plausible (not demonstrated) explanation. Pretraining shows no detectable benefit over random weights. I do not recommend trying DynaMix variants (other windows, embeddings, hidden states) without a new, stated hypothesis. The reference-pool mapping is feasible and the EC&rarr;EO relationship is strongly predictable (largely a shared per-person amplitude level), so any remission test of deviations from it would need to show information beyond that shared level; it was not run.</p><h2>Overview (three figures)</h2>{img("figD3_model_comparison")}{img("figD4_paired_differences")}{img("figD7_representation_stability")}
<h2>1. Cleaning diagnostics (v2 fixed)</h2>
<p>Under v2, recordings changed: {', '.join(f'{k}: {v}' for k, v in av["recordings_status_transitions"].items())}. {av["patients_availability_changed"]} patients had changed E01 feature availability ({av["patients_newly_missing_any_feature"]} newly missing at least one feature, {av["patients_newly_available_any_feature"]} newly available; EC status changed in {av["patients_EC_status_changed"]}, EO in {av["patients_EO_status_changed"]}); {av["changed_patients_remitters"]} of those are remitters. Patient-level table stays private (outputs/v2/availability_changes_PRIVATE.csv).</p>
{img("figD1_conditional_sensitivity")}<p>For Remitter the E01&rarr;E01c AUC change is {SENS[(SENS.endpoint=="Remitter")&(SENS.group=="all patients")].mean_diff.iloc[0]:+.3f} overall, {sensU.mean_diff:+.3f} [{sensU.diff_lo:+.3f}, {sensU.diff_hi:+.3f}] in the {int(sensU.n)} patients with unchanged availability, so the improvement does not hinge on the changed-availability patients; it is concentrated in patients whose features changed more (see figure). This is a conditional descriptive analysis on saved predictions, not causal attribution.</p>
<h3>Component evidence (documentation only; cleaning unchanged)</h3><p>In the {ce["qc_recordings_with_v2_ok"]}-recording outcome-blind QC sample v2 removed {ce["removed_components"]} components; my reconstruction of the ICA application reproduces v2 output exactly ({ce["pipeline_reproduction_exact_all"]}). Stricter documentation categories (computed from the saved table): {CAT['eye_locked']} eye-locked (&ge;5 blinks and blink-locked peak/baseline SD &ge; 3, not drift-like), {CAT['heog_only']} supported only by HEOG correlation (|r| &ge; 0.3), {CAT['drift_like']} drift-like (low-frequency fraction &ge; 0.95), and <b>{CAT['unresolved']}</b> with no supporting eye evidence; {CAT['few_blinks_lt5']} of {CAT['total']} components have fewer than 5 detected blinks. The three non-eye-locked groups are <b>unresolved removals</b> (kept as removed, flagged). Components were not classified from maps alone and nothing was altered.</p>{img("figD2_component_evidence_example1")}{img("figD2_component_evidence_example2")}{img("figD2_component_evidence_example3")}
<h2>2. Frozen DynaMix specification (DYNAMIX_PROTOCOL.md)</h2><p>Weights sha256 <code>{cfgR["weights_sha256"][:16]}&hellip;</code>; K = {cfgR["K"]} gating-noise replicates (chosen by the pre-set criterion on {sb["n_sample_recordings"]} outcome-blind non-rTMS recordings; criterion met by all four models: {sb["criterion_met"]}, so the fallback K=8 applied). Windows: 30 s contiguous, up to 4 per recording, never stitched. Embedding run: {em["tasks"]} (model &times; recording) tasks, wall {em["wall_s"]/60:.0f} min, summed task time {em["summed_task_s"]/3600:.1f} h, mean {em["mean_task_s"]} s per task (K={em["K"]}; runtime scales ~linearly in K and models). Evaluation run time: Remitter {cfgR["runtime_s"]} s, Responder {cfgP["runtime_s"]} s.</p>
<h2>3. Results</h2>{img("figD5_roc_pr")}{img("figD6_calibration")}{tabs}
<h3>Summary and intervals (mean over repeats, conditional bootstrap)</h3>{fmt(SCR[["endpoint","model","auc_s42","auc_s43","auc_s44","mean_auc","mean_auc_lo","mean_auc_hi","gain_vs_E01c","gain_lo","gain_hi","all_gains_positive","triage_pass"]])}<h3>Paired differences</h3>{fmt(PAIR)}
<p><b>Inference:</b> one prespecified permutation test of the pretrained pipeline (Remitter): observed mean AUC {perm["observed_mean_AUC"]:.3f}; {perm["n_perm"]} permutations (rng seed {perm["rng_seed"]}), folds regenerated from permuted labels, all fitting/tuning/threshold steps refit; null mean {perm["null_mean"]:.3f}, 95th percentile {perm["null_q95"]:.3f}; plus-one p = {perm["p_value_plus_one"]:.3f}. This is not a superiority test over E01c and does not address pretraining benefit. Random controls and Responder are descriptive only.</p>
<h2>4. Reference pool and EC&rarr;EO mapping (no outcomes)</h2>{img("figR1_reference_mapping", "Held-out reference people (fixed split): R&sup2; of the ridge EC&rarr;EO mapping versus the training-mean predictor, per output feature (bars with 95% bootstrap intervals over held-out people, conditional on the fixed fit) and versus 20 shuffled-pair controls (grey; mean and min&ndash;max). Positive R&sup2; = better than the training-mean predictor.")}
<p>Pool: {rm["pool_people_listed"]} listed (848 other discovery + 175 workbook-HEALTHY with EC+EO; 1,023 not 1,129 because ADHD-NF/OCD treatment cohorts are excluded); {rm["excluded_missing_EC_or_EO_features"]} excluded for missing EC/EO features, {rm["dropped_exact_duplicate_feature_vectors"]} dropped as exact duplicates, <b>{rm["people_used"]}</b> used ({rm["train_people"]} train / {rm["heldout_people"]} held-out). Ridge alpha {rm["alpha_selected"]} (tuned inside training). Held-out mean R&sup2; <b>{rm["mean_R2"]:.3f}</b> (95% [{rm["mean_R2_ci"][0]:.3f}, {rm["mean_R2_ci"][1]:.3f}]); pooled MSE ratio vs training mean {rm["pooled_mse_ratio_vs_trainmean"]:.3f}; {rm["features_with_R2_gt0"]}/12 outputs beat the mean predictor. Shuffled-pair control: mean R&sup2; {rm["shuffled_mean_R2_mean"]:.3f} (range {rm["shuffled_mean_R2_range"][0]:.3f} to {rm["shuffled_mean_R2_range"][1]:.3f}). A better-than-mean mapping would show that EC predicts EO within this mixed-diagnosis population; it does not show remission information, which was not scored. {fmt(RMF[["feature","mse_model_z","mse_trainmean_z","R2","R2_lo","R2_hi","mse_model_logpower","mse_trainmean_logpower","shuffled_R2_mean"]])}</p>
<h2>5. Failures, limits, reproduction</h2><ul><li>8 patient recordings failed ICA (missing); {int(pd.read_csv(f"{OUT}/dynamix/window_manifest_patients_PRIVATE.csv").query("status=='ok' and n_windows==0").shape[0])} more had no eligible 30-s window; missing conditions were imputed inside training folds.</li><li>In the seed-budget sample 11 of 24 non-rTMS recordings had no eligible window (many bad blocks), so the sample is 13 recordings; K stability for random models failed only on the two gate features.</li><li>DynaMix standardizes each series (amplitude discarded), treats channels independently, and was pretrained on simulated dynamical systems; all EEG-specific choices are mine and frozen in DYNAMIX_PROTOCOL.md.</li><li>Bootstrap intervals are conditional on saved predictions; repeats are not independent patients; cohort previously used.</li><li>Reference-pool features use only 12 log powers; no remission scoring of the EC&rarr;EO extension was run.</li></ul>
<p><b>Reproduce</b> (from first_tests/): <code>scripts/19_pool_features.py; 20_cleaning_diagnostics.py; 21_dynamix_prepare.py patients|seedsample; 22_dynamix_seed_budget.py; 23_dynamix_embed.py; 24_dynamix_eval.py; 27_dynamix_permutation.py; 25_dynamix_analysis.py; 26_reference_mapping.py; 28_dynamix_report.py</code>. Configs: runs/DM_*/config.json (hashes, versions, timestamps).</p>'''
open('DYNAMIX_REPORT.html', 'w').write(html); print('ok', len(html) // 1000, 'KB')
